# Test gap audit after implementation

After **behavioral** implementation and `make test` / `make test-run` / `make test-unit` (or `make test-all`) on a feature branch, run a **test-gap pass** before the code-commenter and documentation passes.

## Required step

1. Scope: branch diff vs `main` under `src/`, `include/`, `tests/`, `Makefile`.
2. Run `sh scripts/check-test-gaps.sh origin/main` without `TEST_GAP_INFORMATIVE` (must exit 0 before draft PR).
3. Delegate to the **test-auditor** subagent ([`test-auditor.md`](../agents/test-auditor.md)) or follow [`testing-gap-auditor` skill](../skills/testing-gap-auditor/SKILL.md).
4. Fix gaps (add unit/snapshot tests) or tune `scripts/check-test-gaps.sh` in a follow-up PR.
5. PR **Test plan** and issue **Testing** subsection must list tests added/updated or one sentence why none.

## Skip when

- Docs/tooling-only: no gameplay/test diff vs `main` (script exits 0)
- User explicitly skips
- Branch diff unchanged since a completed test-gap pass this session

## Workflow order

```text
implement → make test (and related targets) → test-gap pass → code-commenter (if src/ or include/) → documentation pass → draft PR
```

CI runs the same script in **informative** mode (see [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](../../.github/workflows/ci.yml)).

See [agent-workflow.mdc](agent-workflow.mdc) for GitHub steps.
